course: dictionary
lesson: 3228
title: Words that show how
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how something is done. Enthusiastically is an adverb, and it tells you how someone acts. «She clapped enthusiastically» tells you more than «She clapped». The -ly ending is a clue that the word describes an action.
explain: Look at the words around it to find its meaning. «The class nodded enthusiastically when the teacher suggested a trip.» Nodding shows agreement, and the class seems keen, so enthusiastically must mean eagerly and with energy. Try your meaning in the sentence: "The class nodded with excitement when the teacher suggested a trip" still makes sense.
explain: Formal words often appear in school reports. «She takes part enthusiastically in every lesson» means she joins in with energy and eagerness. Swap in your own meaning to check: "She takes part with energy in every lesson." It fits, so you have understood it.
fact: Enthusiastically means with excitement, eagerness and lots of energy.
fact: It can also mean warmly and strongly in favour, as in «The plan was enthusiastically received».
fact: Enthusiastically tells you how someone does an action, such as clapping, nodding or welcoming.
fact: Its forms are enthusiastically, more enthusiastically and most enthusiastically.
fact: School reports use words like this: «contributes enthusiastically» means joins in with energy.
exercise: «The children clapped enthusiastically when the winner was announced.» What does enthusiastically mean here? | Hidden behind the chairs | *With excitement and lots of energy | Angrily and rudely | Slowly and quietly
exercise: «The plan was enthusiastically received.» What does this suggest about how people felt? | Nobody cared about it at all | *They welcomed it warmly and strongly | They were cross and walked out | They lost it on the way home
exercise: «Maya nodded enthusiastically and grabbed her coat.» Find and copy the one word that tells how Maya nodded. | yes | grabbed | *enthusiastically | and
test: Nadia says enthusiastically is just a fancy way of saying happy. Why is that not quite right? | It means happy with no energy at all | It means happy in a quiet, calm way | It is an adjective, so it describes people | *It means with eagerness and energy, showing how someone acts
test: Which word tells you what the team did? «The team cheered enthusiastically at every goal.» | enthusiastically | every | *cheered | goal
exam: Which sentence uses enthusiastically to show how someone acts? | The sky is enthusiastically blue | *Ella enthusiastically sang every verse | Enthusiastically is a big red box | The table is enthusiastically brown
